===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ang|Deoraby}}, of Scandinavian/{{der|en|gmq|-}} origin, from {{der|en|non|Djúra-bý|t=village of the deer}}, from {{m|non|dýr|t=deer}} + {{m|non|bǿr|t=settlement}}. Influenced by [[w:British Latin|British]] {{der|en|la|Derventio}}, the Roman site predating Derby, and possibly also the {{der|en|cel|-}} river name {{m|en|Derwent}}.<ref>Walker, Ian W (2000). Mercia and the Making of England Sutton</ref>

